# Pin LF in the working copy, not just in the blob.
#
# The blobs here are already LF. The problem is the round trip: core.autocrlf
# is true on the Windows machine, so checkout writes CRLF, and the working copy
# -- not a clone -- is what gets uploaded to Google Drive and mounted in Colab.
# Notebooks invoke these launchers directly (`!bash scripts/run_*.sh`), where
# Linux bash does not forgive the CR that Git Bash silently absorbs.
#
# eol=lf makes checkout write LF on every platform, so what reaches Drive is
# what is in the repository.
*.sh text eol=lf
